  "name": "Distorted Time lengthens Decomposition exactly like Eternal (#11350)",
  "contract": "Distorted Time 707553 reads \"Reduces the cooldown of Timerend by $/1000;s2 sec and increases the duration of Decomposition by $/1000;s1 sec\"; Eternal 706777 reads \"... and Decomposition by $/1000;s2 sec\". The Decomposition halves are identical in Spell.dbc: SPELL_AURA_ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER (107), EffectMiscValue 1 SPELLMOD_DURATION, EffectBasePoints 2999 + DieSides 1 = +3000 ms, EffectSpellClassMask [0,524288,0]. Neither talent has a SPELLMOD_ACTIVATION_TIME effect, so neither can change the tick rate. Decomposition 800856 is SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_DAMAGE with Amplitude 4000 and DurationIndex 86 (21000 ms); Aura::CalcMaxDuration applies SPELLMOD_DURATION and AuraEffect::CalculatePeriodic keeps the 4000 ms amplitude. One talent gives 24000 ms, 6 ticks at 4 s; both give 27000 ms, still 6 ticks because a seventh would need 28000 ms. The report's 7-tick expectation is not in either tooltip. Regression guard for behaviour that already works (#11350).",
